+### Fixed
+
+- **Editor crash when closing a MIDI port whose device is gone** (Reconnect,
+  entering play mode, recompiling — after a controller dropped off USB). On
+  WinMM, RtMidi 6.0 leaves a port half-closed when `midiInUnprepareHeader`
+  fails, and freeing it then deletes its buffers twice : heap corruption, or
+  `std::terminate`. Closing before freeing was not enough. A port whose close
+  fails is now quarantined — kept, never freed — at the cost of a few KB per
+  incident.
+
